      "content": "I completely understand the appeal of a natural solution, but even taking St. John's Wort every other day with Lexapro is a gamble—it still significantly alters how your body processes the medication. That online advice about it being \"gentle\" overlooks that as a plant, it contains active compounds that can cause severe interactions with prescription drugs. One week of trying it could lead to lasting, dangerous side effects like serotonin syndrome, which is a medical emergency. Please, prioritize your safety, and have an honest conversation with your prescriber about why you're not feeling relief yet—they can offer safer, targeted alternatives.",
      "source": "target",
